    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded `checkDigit` = a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`, exposed on the owner response.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (integer, 0\u20139, read-only), right after `customerCode`. The `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec, so this gives the response a `checkDigit` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired the new field via a MapStruct `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and added a `checkDigit(Owner)` helper implementing the standard Luhn algorithm over the digit characters of `customerCode` (ignoring the `-` separators), returning `null` when no code is assigned.\n\nThis mirrors the existing pattern for other derived read-only fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`) rather than storing anything new on the entity. The test recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` and the full suite pass.",
